@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch17ch18-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch17ch18-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 17 and 18"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch17ch18-lineage/1.0.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch17ch18_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.0.0 (2026-11-11): Mission stage only (one stage per version, as Lineage3-6 learned). Opened on the owner's instruction 2026-11-11 ('Give me the chapters 15 & 16. After that start for chapters 17 & 18').
ORDINAL AND ONE-AT-A-TIME CHECK: the latest version of every lineage file was read; ordinals 3 to 6 are taken in the narrow-lineage files and 1 to 4 in the slides register (different namespace); the next free ordinal is 7. Lineage5 (ch13-14) had been left InProgress with every item Done and Lineage6 opened beside it; that breach was found and cured first (Lineage5 closed LS_Achieved with its closure report, owner-confirmed, commit 189628b). Lineage6 is LS_Achieved. Lineage3 (ch9-10) is still open with one carried-forward item (TK_Ret_Ch09_Research/_Verify), a pre-existing state not changed here and reported to the owner.
STATE-CHECK PRECEDING THIS OPENING (live files, not memory): chapter 17 (PDF and Word Documents): deck SEN0414_Ch17_PDFAndWordDocuments_3e_v2_0_0.pptx (58 slides), page v9_96_0, manifest chapter_code_ch17_v1_0_0.json (28 examples), stories script 6 stories, resources slide 14 links. Chapter 18 (CSV, JSON, XML): deck v2_0_1 (53 slides; v2_0_0 superseded, the register's control verdict names v2_0_1), page v9_96_0, manifest chapter_code_ch18_v1_0_1.json (27 examples), stories 6, resources 14 links. Both chapters went through repair cycles in October under the old process (ch17 page v9_95_0 failed page test 9.37.0 on a Pillow module left None, repaired as v9_96_0; ch18 page v9_95_0 failed the leak probe and story-layout probe, repaired as template 9.52.4 and v9_96_0); the final page checks pass (Page/Ch17 PASS 402 features, Page/Ch18 PASS 400, ch17 width 1366/1400/390 PASS, ch17 leak probe seed 5 PASS). The register records the Research, Deck_Build and Page_Build tasks of both chapters Done. No legacy YA duplicate decks exist for these subjects. rdodi/ research-artifact folders exist for both chapters and are out of scope, as in Lineage6."""@en .

ex:ProfileDecl7 a backlog:ProfileDeclaration ;
    rdfs:label "Profile: AAL (agentic adaptive), default"@en ;
    backlog:declaresProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:declaresLevel backlog:Level_L2 ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Default ;
    backlog:hasDeclarationRationale "Same declaration as Lineage3 to Lineage6: work is executed by an LLM agent, no human team; AAL is the default profile for agent-executed work. Level L2 stated plainly." ;
    backlog:declaredAt "2026-11-11T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:reviewDate "2026-11-15"^^xsd:date .

ex:Lineage7 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 17 and 18, narrow lineage"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission7 ; backlog:lineageOrdinal 7 ; backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Opened ;
    backlog:hasProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:followsProfileDeclaration ex:ProfileDecl7 ;
    backlog:continuesFrom ex:Lineage2 ;
    rdfs:comment "ex:Lineage2 (sen0414-slides-lineage namespace) is the closed slides lineage this continues from, as Lineage3 to Lineage6 do; chapters 17 and 18's retrofit was recorded Done there."@en .

ex:Mission7 a backlog:Mission ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 17 and 18 taught from one approved draft each"@en ;
    backlog:missionFor ex:Backlog7 ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "Chapters 17 (PDF and Word Documents) and 18 (CSV, JSON and XML) of the third edition are taught with a deck and an interactive page, each produced from one owner-approved chapter draft, following the same review given to chapters 9 to 16: a true, sourced story per concept the chapter teaches, an accurate resources slide, and any open item named and closed before build." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin "Owner's instruction 2026-11-11, following the Lineage3 to Lineage6 pattern and their stated exclusion that later chapter pairs get their own narrow lineages." .
